	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>CTRL_PI_AR</h1>

<h2>🇩🇪 Deutsch</h2>

<p>AR-Adapter-Wrapper um <code>OSCAT::Basic::POUs::Engineering::Control::CTRL_PI</code>. Istwert (<code>AR_ACT</code>), Sollwert (<code>SET</code>), Rauschunterdrueckung/Offset (<code>SUP</code>/<code>OFS</code>), Handwert (<code>M_I</code>), Handbetrieb-Umschaltung (<code>AX_MAN</code>), Reglerparameter (<code>KP</code>/<code>KI</code>) UND Grenzwerte (<code>LL</code>/<code>LH</code>) sind als Adapter-Sockets ausgefuehrt, in derselben Reihenfolge wie die InputVars des umschlossenen CTRL_PI - jeder loest bei Ankunft eines neuen Werts <code>CTRL_PI.REQ</code> aus. Kein explizites <code>REQ</code>-Event mehr noetig, da jeder Socket selbst triggert. <code>RST</code> (Reset des Integrators) bleibt als eigenes Event erhalten.</p>

<h3>Reine Adapter-Grenze</h3>

<ul>
	<li><strong>AR_ACT</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): Istwert (REAL, z. B. von <code>FT_DERIV_10_AR.AR_OUT</code>)</li>
	<li><strong>SET</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): Sollwert (REAL, dynamisch berechnet, z. B. Fahrgeschwindigkeit*Voreilung)</li>
	<li><strong>SUP</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): Rauschunterdrueckung (REAL, dynamisch)</li>
	<li><strong>OFS</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): Offset (REAL, dynamisch)</li>
	<li><strong>M_I</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): Handwert (REAL, dynamisch)</li>
	<li><strong>AX_MAN</strong> (Socket, <code>AX</code>): Handbetrieb-Umschaltung (optional, z. B. von <code>AX_T_FF.Q</code>)</li>
	<li><strong>KP</strong>/<strong>KI</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): Reglerparameter (REAL, dynamisch)</li>
	<li><strong>LL</strong>/<strong>LH</strong> (Socket, <code>AR</code>): unterer/oberer Grenzwert (REAL, dynamisch)</li>
	<li><strong>AR_Y</strong> (Plug, <code>AR</code>): Stellwert (REAL, z. B. zur Weitergabe an <code>AR_TO_AD_NUM.AR_IN</code>)</li>
	<li><strong>AR_DIFF</strong> (Plug, <code>AR</code>): Regelabweichung (<code>DIFF = SET - ACT</code>, REAL)</li>
	<li><strong>AB_LIM</strong> (Plug, <code>AB</code>): Begrenzung aktiv Flag (<code>LIM</code>, BOOL)</li>
</ul>

<h2>🇬🇧 English</h2>

<p>AR-adapter wrapper around <code>OSCAT::Basic::POUs::Engineering::Control::CTRL_PI</code>. Actual value (<code>AR_ACT</code>), set point (<code>SET</code>), noise suppression/offset (<code>SUP</code>/<code>OFS</code>), manual value (<code>M_I</code>), manual mode switch (<code>AX_MAN</code>), controller gains (<code>KP</code>/<code>KI</code>) AND limits (<code>LL</code>/<code>LH</code>) are all adapter sockets, in the same order as the wrapped CTRL_PI's own InputVars, each triggering <code>CTRL_PI.REQ</code> on arrival - no explicit <code>REQ</code> event needed any more, since every socket triggers itself. <code>RST</code> (integrator reset) remains its own event. Control output (<code>AR_Y</code>), control error (<code>AR_DIFF</code>) and limit flag (<code>AB_LIM</code>) are adapter plugs.</p>
]]></Attribute>
</FBType>
